      "reason": "The question asks for bias, RMSE, spatial correlation and depth-by-depth means on the GLODAP grid, so the fields must share one comparison mask over cells where both model and GLODAP are defined.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all fields on the GLODAP 1° grid and apply one shared mask from `build_comparison_mask` before the map bias/RMSE/correlation; the reference is GLODAP, not WOA23, so pass `ocean_only=False` (the default `ocean_only=True` silently drops GLODAP cells that WOA23 calls land and flatters every model). Report the mask's cell counts.",
        "The question asks the depth-profile bias per model over \"every cell where that model and GLODAP are both defined at that depth\": that pairwise mask is followed as stated, but each model's depth-profile numbers then come from a different sample, so they must not be ranked on those numbers."
