      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The question requires DIC and alkalinity in micromoles per kilogram while CMIP6 BGC tracers are stored per volume, so the per-mass conversion and variable-specific scale factors must be applied.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert model `dissic`/`talk` as µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ using in-situ density from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`, passed to `transform_unit` (its constant default errs ~1 % in the deep ocean and fresh polar water); state `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "GLODAP is already µmol kg-1; converting mol m-3 by ×1e3 gives mmol m-3 = µmol L-1, still per volume, and is not comparable until divided by density."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The question asks for global 0–50 m means and global depth-level bias means, so the appropriate area/volume weighting over ocean cells must be used rather than an unweighted cell average.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Every global 0-50 m mean must be weighted over the same valid cells: `op='volume_weighted_mean'` for means whose dimensions include depth, `op='area_weighted_mean'` for horizontal ones; a plain mean over a lat-lon grid over-weights polar cells and unweighted level-by-level averaging is wrong.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default and `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`; the difference of the separately-taken per-source 0-50 m means is not the shared-mask map bias, and the answer must say so."
      ]
    },
